        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Frears, Christopher Hampton, John Malkovich, Glenn Close, Uma Thurman, Pierre Choderlos de Laclos\n- Works: Mary Reilly, Dangerous Liaisons, Les liaisons dangereuses, Les Liaisons dangereuses, Savages, British Vogue\n- Topics: film adaptation, re-teaming, historical drama\n\nFacts:\n- Pierre Choderlos de Laclos wrote the 18th-century French novel \"Les Liaisons dangereuses.\"\n- Christopher Hampton wrote the play \"Savages.\"\n- Christopher Hampton's play \"Les liaisons dangereuses\" was a theatrical adaptation of Pierre Choderlos de Laclos's novel \"Les Liaisons dangereuses.\"\n- Uma Thurman appeared on the December 1985 and May 1986 covers of British \"Vogue.\"\n- \"Dangerous Liaisons\" is a 1988 American historical drama film based on Christopher Hampton's play \"Les liaisons dangereuses.\"\n- Uma Thurman starred in \"Dangerous Liaisons\" in 1988.\n- Stephen Frears, Christopher Hampton, John Malkovich, and Glenn Close were all involved in the Oscar-winning 1988 film \"Dangerous Liaisons.\"\n- \"Mary Reilly\" re-teamed director Stephen Frears, screenwriter Christopher Hampton, and actors John Malkovich and Glenn Close after their work on \"Dangerous Liaisons.\"",
